{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Like the days of the tree.</b> That it will stand for many years, like the carob tree, and others." "And the meaning of <b>and the work of their hands will grow old before My chosen ones</b>: for there are works that a man makes and grows old, and they will appear new like a building and a document. <small>(And they)</small> <b>bekhiri</b> (before My chosen ones): they are workers."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {1 "Reading בחירי as the lemma from the verse ('My chosen ones'); the final clause 'they are workers' likely glosses בחירי by re-parsing it, though the argument is cryptic."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:07.222432277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}